1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,220
If your Unboarding page does not launch automatically, go to the bottom left in Applications -> Accessories -> djibian-unboarding.

2
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:11,940
Once launched, click on <Set up your OpenPGP security key ID>.

3
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:12,980
I confirm.

4
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:14,240
Do you have a key? <Yes>.

5
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:14,960
Insert it.

6
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:16,100
Click <Yes>.

7
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:17,000
It is detected.

8
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:17,740
<Continue>.

9
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:18,960
Do you have the QR codes? <No>.

10
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:21,260
<Create my OpenPGP identity>.

11
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:21,880
<I confirm>.

12
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:28,340
Enter your birth last name, first name, date of birth, and finally your country of birth.

13
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:30,180
Continue.

14
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:32,540
Here, enter your email.

15
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:35,620
Then, continue.

16
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:36,880
Check your information.

17
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:37,980
Continue.

18
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:39,740
Click <Print>.

19
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:41,060
Print your QR codes.

20
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:42,900
Once done, click <Continue>.

21
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:43,640
I confirm.

22
00:00:43,740 --> 00:00:45,040
You can see that your key is detected.

23
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:45,620
Continue.

24
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,080
Do you have the QR codes? <Yes>.

25
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:47,960
Scan them.

26
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:51,740
Here, we see the first, the second, and the last.

27
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:54,520
<Save>.

28
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:55,620
And there you go, your key is created.
